            <ArticleTitle>Plasmatic beta-endorphin levels and thalamic surgery for pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>35-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Plasma beta-endorphin levels were found to be significantly lower in patients suffering from chronic pain of malignant etiology than in a control group. After a bilateral stereotactic cryothalamotomy in Centrum Medianum and Parafascicularis nuclei, a good clinical result and a significant increase in plasma beta-endorphin levels were obtained.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
